// Laser grid -- real beams, not a painted lattice.
//
// A sweep band FILL patterns the band where it touches a surface, so the lines
// are on the walls and there is nothing in the air between them: walk into it
// and you walk through a picture. Each line here is an actual segment of light
// -- lit per pixel by distance from it, visible hanging in space, occluded
// correctly by geometry, and blooming on its own.
//
// The two are meant to be used together. The fill goes around corners and up
