// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What is drawn inside a sweep band.
//
// A band knows two things about every pixel it covers: how strongly it covers
// it, and where that pixel IS. It used to discard the second, so a band could
// only be a wash. Every shape that defines a distance also implies two tangent
// coordinates -- in a corridor, height and across -- and a pattern is just a
// function of those two.
//
// SPACING 0 IN AN AXIS MEANS NO LINES IN THAT AXIS. That is why there is no
// separate mode for slats or for a single tripwire: they are a grid with one
// spacing zeroed.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

